{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'term_tracker_item|IAO_0000233|3597|issue' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"3746:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 cl:has_high_plasma_membrane_amount <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1481>)\n3754:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 cl:has_low_plasma_membrane_amount <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1481>)\n3808:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000003 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2124>)\n3856:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000009 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000079 from Plant Ontology instead. An elongated cell with approximately wedge-shaped ends, found in the vascular cambium, which gives rise to the elements of the axial system in the secondary vascular tissues.\")\n3908:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0000015 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/574\")\n4113:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17289566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1038/sj.eye.6700575\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000036 \"A somatic stem cell that is committed to an epithelial fate, possessing the capacity for self-renewal and the ability to differentiate into one or more distinct mature cell types of the epithelial lineage. This cell is crucial for the development, homeostasis, repair, and regeneration of epithelial tissues.\")\n4331:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000054 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2698>)\n4340:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000055 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2922\")\n4362:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D005347\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibroblast\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000057 \"A connective tissue cell which secretes an extracellular matrix rich in collagen and other macromolecules. Flattened and irregular in outline with branching processes; appear fusiform or spindle-shaped.\")\n4376:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000058 \"Skeletogenic cell that is typically non-terminally differentiated, secretes an avascular, GAG rich matrix; is not buried in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, located adjacent to cartilage tissue (including within the perichondrium), and develops from prechondroblast (and thus prechondrogenic) cell.\")\n4434:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D010006\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000062 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes osteoid, is capable of producing mineralized (hydroxyapatite) matrix, is located adjacent to or within osteoid tissue, and arises from the transformation of a preosteoblast cell.\")\n4529:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000073 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1149>)\n4557:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000077 \"A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.\")\n4581:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000080 \"A cell which moves among different tissues of the body, via blood, lymph, or other medium.\")\n4633:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000085 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1935>)\n4641:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000086 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1935>)\n4649:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000087 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1935>)\n4657:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000088 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1935>)\n4665:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000089 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1935>)\n4673:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000090 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1935>)\n4681:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007728\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771589\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17105582\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000091 \"A tissue-resident macrophage of the reticuloendothelial system found on the luminal surface of the hepatic sinusoids involved in erythrocyte clearance. Markers include F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68-positive, sialoadhesin-positive, CD163/SRCR-positive. Irregular, with long processes including lamellipodia extending into the sinusoid lumen, have flattened nucleus with cytoplasm containing characteristic invaginations of the plasma membrane (vermiform bodies); lie within the sinusoid lumen attached to the endothelial surface; derived from the bone marrow, form a major part of the body's mononuclear phagocyte system.\")\n4697:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10428500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15055519\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17380158\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000092 \"A specialized phagocytic cell associated with the absorption and removal of the mineralized matrix of bone tissue, which typically differentiates from monocytes. This cell has the following markers: tartrate-resistant acid phosphatase type 5-positive, PU.1-positive, c-fos-positive, nuclear factor NF-kappa-B p100 subunit-positive, tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 11A-positive and macrophage colony-stimulating factor 1 receptor-positive.\")\n4703:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000092 \"Morphology: Highly vesicular; markers: Surface: RANK, cFMS (MCSF receptor); Secreted: cathepsin K and TRAP (tartate resistant acid phosphatase); transcription factors: PU.1, cFOS, MITF, NFkB (p52); role or process: tissue remodelling: bone resorption; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n4761:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008407\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2855166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15153310\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16455980\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19671378\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:212366338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000097 \"A cell that is found in almost all tissues containing numerous basophilic granules and capable of releasing large amounts of histamine and heparin upon activation. Progenitors leave bone marrow and mature in connective and mucosal tissue. Mature mast cells are found in all tissues, except the bloodstream. Their phenotype is CD117-high, CD123-negative, CD193-positive, CD200R3-positive, and FceRI-high. Stem-cell factor (KIT-ligand; SCF) is the main controlling signal of their survival and development.\")\n4768:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000097 \"tissue basophil\")\n4894:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000111 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1069>)\n5020:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000124 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/715>)\n5033:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000125 \"Not all glial cells develop from glioblasts, with microglia developing from the mesoderm instead. See https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/1571\")\n5109:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21976958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23284695\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34741068\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36769303\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000132 \"An hexagonal, flattened, mitochondria-rich endothelial cell that forms a monolayer on the posterior surface of the cornea (the corneal endothelium). Corneal endothelial cells are derived from the neural crest and are responsible for keeping the cornea transparent by maintaining the tissue in a semi-dry state through the action of their ionic pumps and tight junction barrier.\")\n5119:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000133 \"Ectoderm destined to be nervous tissue.\")\n5126:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2613570\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10102814\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16923606\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17986482\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19960544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesenchymal_stem_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=mesenchymal%20stem%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000134 \"A connective tissue cell that normally gives rise to other cells that are organized as three-dimensional masses. In humans, this cell type is CD73-positive, CD90-positive, CD105-positive, CD45-negative, CD34-negative, and MHCII-negative. They may further differentiate into osteoblasts, adipocytes, myocytes, neurons, or chondroblasts in vitro. Originally described as residing in the bone marrow, this cell type is now known to reside in many, if not all, adult organs.\")\n5144:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0000134 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/474\")\n5164:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017667\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000136 \"A fat-storing cell found mostly in the abdominal cavity and subcutaneous tissue of mammals. Fat is usually stored in the form of triglycerides.\")\n5191:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32491508\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000138 \"A skeletogenic cell that secretes a specialized, avascular, GAG-rich matrix, is embedded in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, and develops from a chondroblast cell.\")\n5212:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000140 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes dentine matrix, is derived from odontogenic papilla. Embedded in dentine tissue, and is the transformation of a non-terminally differentiated odontoblast cell.\")\n5395:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000161 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/427>)\n5598:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000181 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/720>)\n5855:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000212 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/2271>)\n5862:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000213 \"OBSOLETE. A cell within an epithelial cell sheet whose main function is to act as an internal or external covering for a tissue or an organism.\")\n5863:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000213 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3014>)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
